<li>PostgreSQL 18, <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/tutorial-transactions.html">Transactions</a> and <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/transaction-iso.html">Transaction Isolation</a>: atomicity, Read Committed snapshots, waiting updates and rechecking their conditions. <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/sql-update.html">UPDATE</a> defines RETURNING.</li>
<li>PostgreSQL 18, <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/libpq-exec.html#LIBPQ-PQEXECPARAMS">Command Execution Functions</a>: passing parameter values separately from SQL text. OWASP, <a href="https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Authorization_Cheat_Sheet.html">Authorization Cheat Sheet</a>: checking which records a caller may access.</li>
<li>PostgreSQL 18, <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/using-explain.html">Using EXPLAIN</a>, <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/indexes-intro.html">Introduction to Indexes</a>, <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/storage-page-layout.html">Database Page Layout</a> and <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/runtime-config-resource.html">Resource Consumption</a>: plans, page access, shared buffers and working memory.</li>
<li>PostgreSQL 18, <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/wal-intro.html">Write-Ahead Logging</a>, <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/runtime-config-wal.html">WAL settings</a> and <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/protocol-flow.html">Message Flow</a>: durable commit, relaxed acknowledgement and connection loss at the transaction boundary.</li>
<li>PostgreSQL 18, <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/warm-standby.html">Log-Shipping Standby Servers</a>, <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/warm-standby-failover.html">Failover</a> and <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/continuous-archiving.html">Continuous Archiving and Point-in-Time Recovery</a>: replica milestones, writer authority and recovery to an earlier state.</li>
<li>SQLite, <a href="https://www.sqlite.org/serverless.html">SQLite Is Serverless</a>, <a href="https://www.sqlite.org/whentouse.html">Appropriate Uses For SQLite</a> and <a href="https://www.sqlite.org/isolation.html">Isolation In SQLite</a>: embedded execution, sharing and the single-writer boundary.</li>
<li>AWS Well-Architected Framework, <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/rel_planning_for_recovery_objective_defined_recovery.html">Define recovery objectives for downtime and data loss</a>: RTO and RPO as workload requirements.</li>
<li>Amazon Builders’ Library, <a href="https://aws.amazon.com/builders-library/making-retries-safe-with-idempotent-APIs/">Making retries safe with idempotent APIs</a>, and AWS Prescriptive Guidance, <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/cloud-design-patterns/transactional-outbox.html">Transactional outbox pattern</a>: stable request identities, changed parameters and durable external work.</li>
<li>CockroachDB, <a href="https://docs.cockroachlabs.com/docs/stable/architecture/replication-layer">Replication Layer</a> and <a href="https://docs.cockroachlabs.com/docs/stable/architecture/transaction-layer">Transaction Layer</a>: replicated ranges and atomic decisions across them. DuckDB, <a href="https://duckdb.org/why_duckdb">Why DuckDB</a>: an embedded column-oriented SQL engine for analytical work.</li>
</ul>
</section>

